# Ghostty, declared the way ncurses actually listens.
#
# xterm-ghostty says Tc and keeps colors#256. Tc is a tmux convention that
# ncurses ignores; ncurses enters direct-colour mode only on the RGB
# capability. So an ncurses program under xterm-ghostty cannot be handed a
# 24-bit colour and approximates to the 256 palette -- visibly close, and not
# the same: gruvbox #1d2021 comes out as #1c1c1c.
#
# The first use= wins, so this takes the colour machinery -- RGB,
# colors#0x1000000 and the direct setaf/setab -- from xterm-direct, and
# everything else from xterm-ghostty.
#
# The name must keep the xterm prefix. Ghostty's own config comment says it
# sets TERM to xterm-ghostty rather than ghostty precisely because vim looks
# for that prefix to enable modifyOtherKeys.
#
# Compile with an ncurses 6.1+ tic, and say where it goes. The tic shipped in
# macOS is 6.0 and cannot store colors#0x1000000: it clamps it to 32767
# without complaining, and the result paints garbage like ESC[38;5;8154980m.
# Without -o it installs into $TERMINFO, which here is inside the Ghostty app
# bundle, where an update would wipe it.
#
#   /opt/homebrew/opt/ncurses/bin/tic -x -o ~/.terminfo \
#       ~/.config/ghostty/xterm-ghostty-direct.info
#
# Do NOT make this the global TERM on a system that also has an older ncurses.
# colors#0x1000000 only fits the extended terminfo format, which arrived in
# ncurses 6.1, and 6.0 does not report a partial read -- it says "unknown
# terminal" and the program falls back to nothing. macOS ships 6.0 and every
# tool in /usr/bin links it: measured on 2026-08-18, `TERM=xterm-ghostty-direct
# less` prints "WARNING: terminal is not fully functional" and vi degrades.
#
# So point only the programs that need it at this entry:
#
#   alias dvtm='TERM=xterm-ghostty-direct dvtm'
#
# On a system with one modern ncurses everywhere, setting it globally is fine
# (Ghostty: `term = xterm-ghostty-direct`).
#
# To undo: remove the entry from ~/.terminfo.
xterm-ghostty-direct|ghostty with ncurses direct color,
	use=xterm-direct,
	use=xterm-ghostty,
